TITLE:: RLTimeMap
summary:: A map of time, t to a t + b: a shift, a stretch
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLTimePoints, Classes/RLPulse, Classes/RLTimeSpans, Classes/RLNetwork, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
Every time point t sent to a t + b. A shift (a = 1) and a stretch (b = 0) are the automorphisms of the time points with their pulses (Popoff and Yust): a shift changes no pulse, a stretch by a multiplies every period by a. Applied to a metre network (link::Classes/RLNetwork#-transformedBy::) a shift is a displacement, a stretch an augmentation; given to link::Classes/RLNetwork#-isMorphismTo:: it is how the context is moved on the way.

It is the left element code::[b, a]:: of link::Classes/RLTimeSpans::, acting on points in place of spans. A value.

code::
~later = RLTimeMap(1, 1/12);            // a sixteenth of a 6/8 bar later
~later.value(5/2);                      // 31/12
~later.onArrow(RLPulse(1/2));           // RLPulse(1/2)
RLTimeMap(2, 0).onArrow(RLPulse(1/2));  // RLPulse(1): twice as slow
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: a
The stretch; 0 is an Error. A negative one turns time round.
argument:: b
The shift.

